---
import "../sternzeit/sternzeit.css";
import "./dunstkreis.css";
import "./clocks.css";
import Fig from "../Fig.astro";

const SCENARIOS = [
    ["skybox", "Skybox", "Everything computed once, kept as a cube map and nine numbers"],
    ["live", "Live sky", "The sky pass every frame, the sky view whenever the Sun moves"],
    ["lit", "Lighting a scene", "A live sky that also lights a scene by its cube map and coefficients"],
    ["aerial", "Aerial perspective", "Lighting a scene, and the air in front of it by the aerial perspective volume"],
];
---

<figure class="strip-figure wide" id="clocks">
    <div class="clocks-bar">
        <span class="steps" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Scenario">
            {
                SCENARIOS.map(([value, text, title]) => (
                    <label title={title}>
                        <input type="radio" name="clocks-scenario" value={value} checked={value === "lit"} />
                        <span>{text}</span>
                    </label>
                ))
            }
        </span>
    </div>
    <div class="strip-panel clocks-panel">
        <svg role="img" aria-label="The pieces of dunstkreis, what each reads, how large it is and when it runs"></svg>
    </div>
    <p class="clocks-measured note" data-field="measured"></p>
    <figcaption class="figure-caption">
        Four pieces, four clocks: every texture and buffer dunstkreis computes, each in the lane of what makes it run
        again. A box shows what it holds, read from this page's own textures and shown as in the figures that explain
        them, the aerial perspective by its middle and its last slice, then its size in texels and its memory, textures
        at four half floats per texel. An arrow leads to what reads it, and every pass below the tables reads both, but
        the one computing the coefficients. Dashed, what is yours. A scenario lights up what it runs, and a skybox runs
        it all once. The timings are measured on this GPU as the page loaded, at the sizes the tables
        (<Fig id="tables" />) and the cube map (<Fig id="environment" />) are set to, the sky pass into a full HD frame;
        under the figure, their sums for each occasion.
    </figcaption>
</figure>

<script>
    import "./clocks";
</script>
